# Line endings are part of the evidence here.
#
# The REX-803 material package is verified by SHA256 over exact bytes, and it is read on a different
# host than the one that produced it. With core.autocrlf=true a checkout would rewrite LF to CRLF, so
# the reviewer would hash bytes that differ from the ones the index lists and report a mismatch that
# belongs to the checkout rather than to the material. These files are therefore stored and checked
# out verbatim: the blob bytes are the bytes that were hashed.
mission-book/reports/REX-803/evidence/** -text
# REX-805 publishes the same exact-byte receipt/index contract across hosts.
mission-book/reports/REX-805/evidence/** -text
